  "id": "cortisol",
  "term": "cortisol",
  "definition": "Cortisol is a measurable substance in saliva that researchers use as a physiological indicator when studying stress and well-being. In this study, lower salivary cortisol concentrations after the interaction were associated with reduced perceived stress.",
